    "schema_diff_summary": "fuzzy.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Change only camel_bonus. Replace is_ascii_lowercase with is_lowercase. Replace is_ascii_uppercase with is_uppercase. Keep the one && condition. Index 0 still returns 0. Do not nest an if inside an if.  Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch boundary_bonus, digit_hump, gap_adjust, or fuzzy_match. The existing test a_camel_hump_adds_eight stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_unicode_camel_hump_adds_eight uses fuzzy_match of e acute and the text a then capital E acute. The score is 24. The positions are 1. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
